# Git flow for pier

Repository: https://github.com/fsantos12/pier (repo not created yet)

## Long-lived branches
- `main`, `test` and `dev` must be protected (ruleset to create with the repo):
  pull request required, no force pushes, no deletion. Never push to them directly.
- Promotion order: `feature/<name>` -> `dev` -> `test` -> `main`.

## Short-lived branches
- `feature/<name>`: cut from `dev`, merged into `dev` by PR.
  `<name>` is short kebab-case and matches the blueprint header (e.g. `feature/core`).
- `hotfix/<name>`: cut from `main`, merged by PR into `main`, then `test`, then `dev`.
  Every hotfix carries a regression test (Hunter Pier).

## Who does what
- Filipe commits and pushes code.
- Dever Pier may also commit and push, but only to `feature/*` branches, never to
  `main`, `test` or `dev`. Keep commits small and post the touched files in the
  pier group after each push.
- No other bot pushes to the repository.
- Gittie Pier creates branches and opens every PR with a descriptive summary,
  flagging breaking changes and security notes. Filipe approves and merges or rejects.
- Dever Pier shares snippets in chat, or pushes them to the feature branch when Filipe is away.
- Rule files prepared by bots in /workspace/pier are pushed by Filipe.

## Per-feature order
1. Stormie Pier: blueprint approved, names the `feature/<name>` branch.
2. Gittie Pier: creates the branch from `dev` and announces it in the group.
3. Filipe codes (Dever Pier helps on request).
4. Hunter Pier: unit tests and clippy pass (gate for feature -> dev).
5. Cleanie Pier: cleanup pass on the feature branch.
6. Gittie Pier: opens the PR into `dev`.
7. Before `dev` -> `test`: integration and stress tests pass (Hunter Pier).

## Commits and PRs
- Commit messages and PR text in English, imperative mood ("Add query AST").
- One feature per PR; delete the feature branch after merge.
